{
    "id": 72,
    "title": "Domain sales get their own switch",
    "why": "Jason, 2026-11-17: \"I did say domains where to be separated from storefronts right. Finding and buying was to be its own process.\" Release #71 opened Shop → Domains, the Domains tab and the wallet's domain charges on DOMAINS_MODE, the storefront's \"Own domains on storefronts\" setting. A new setting, DOMAIN_SALES_MODE (\"Domain sales\": off, test or live; on the Name.com card), now alone governs them; DOMAINS_MODE means only the storefront's Connect your domain again. Every safety rule carries over: test mode (our team only), test accounts and the staging copy use Name.com's and QuickBooks' sandboxes; live sales are refused while NAMECOM_ENV is sandbox; Name.com refusing us shows the paused message. A domain sale's Name.com calls now follow the sales switch only, so the storefront switch's test mode can never send a live sale to the sandbox, or the reverse. The Name.com card shows both switches. One FAQ entry added.",
